    "credit":  "OCHA Humanitarian Icons (un-ocha.github.io/humanitarian-icons), CC0 1.0",
    "plain":  "Public domain, dedicated under Creative Commons Zero 1.0 (CC0): you may copy, change and share these icons for any purpose, also commercially, without asking and without giving credit. The repository\u0027s LICENSE is the CC0 1.0 legal code. OCHA says it does not intend an official meaning for the icons and that their meaning and representation do not imply acceptance or endorsement by the United Nations; this pack is not endorsed by OCHA or the United Nations, and it contains no UN emblem.",
    "ask":  "While attribution is not required, we would appreciate: Crediting OCHA where feasible.",
    "askFrom":  "https://github.com/UN-OCHA/humanitarian-icons/blob/main/README.md",
    "how":  "No credit is required, and SiliCoDraw adds no credit line for these icons. OCHA appreciates a credit where feasible (Page → Copy full icon credits gives a line for it) and, for its records, an email to ochavisual@un.org with a link to your webpage or publication; both are up to you.",
    "changes":  "Converted from SVG to SiliCoDraw\u0027s icon format, one color version only (black; the UN-blue and white files are the same drawings, and SiliCoDraw recolors icons): fitted into a 100 × 100 box, style sheets written out as attributes, coordinates rounded, and the color made recolorable. Each icon was drawn and compared with the original on a white and on a dark page. Names are the file names in words, in American spelling. The groups are SiliCoDraw\u0027s, since the repository has none. Left out: user-interface and file-type symbols, the plain status marks, icons whose meaning is lettering (NGO, NFI), icons of conflict, violence and the military, religious buildings, and the icons with UN lettering.",
